# Component Standards

Use the current project structure as source of truth:

- `src/app`: app composition (router, providers, layout, stores)
- `src/features`: feature-specific pages/components
- `src/shared/components/ui`: reusable UI base (shadcn/radix)
- `src/shared/components/states`: reusable app states (loading/error/missing params)
- `src/shared/{hooks,http,lib,schemas,utils}`: shared logic and contracts

Follow naming and code patterns:

- File names in `kebab-case` (`app.layout.tsx`, `use-item.ts`, `*.schema.ts`)
- Components in `PascalCase`, variables/functions in `camelCase`
- Always type props, function params, and return values
- Prefer `import type` for type-only imports

Component and hook rules:

- Reuse existing shared components before creating new ones
- Keep business-specific UI inside the feature folder
- Split large components into focused subcomponents/hooks
- Custom hooks must start with `use*`
- Validate external inputs (props, query params, handler params) with guard clauses/Zod

Styling and imports:

- Use Tailwind utility classes and `cn()` for class merging
- Use `cva` for variant-heavy components
- Import order: external packages -> `@/` aliases -> relative imports

